ec: clear stale needs_reconcile on non-degraded stripes in stripe_repair

bch2_stripe_repair() early-returns success for stripes that are not
degraded, leaving needs_reconcile set. But needs_reconcile on a stripe can
only ever transition back to 0 by rewriting the stripe - which only happens
on this same repair path, behind the stripe_degraded() check:

- bch2_bkey_needs_reconcile() (fs/data/reconcile/trigger.c) returns true for
  a stripe only when (need_rb & data_replicas) && !needs_reconcile, so for a
  flagged-but-healthy stripe it returns 0 and bch2_bkey_set_needs_reconcile()
  bails before set_needs_reconcile_stripe() could clear the flag.
- fsck's check_reconcile_work only validates the opposite direction
  (stripe_needs_reconcile_not_set).

So a stripe flagged during a transient device state (bad/evacuating device
later returning, durability churn) is reprocessed by every reconcile pass
forever: ret == 0, no IO, no state change, and the reconcile_hipri entry and
its accounting ("stripes pending" in reconcile status / fs usage) never go
away. Observed on a 10-device pool: ~445k flagged stripes, reconcile_stripe
counter in the petabytes, zero bytes moved, all other reconcile work starved.

Fix: when the stripe turns out not to be degraded, write it back with
needs_reconcile cleared. The stripe trigger then drops the reconcile_hipri
work entry and the pending-stripe accounting.

diff --git a/fs/data/ec/create.c b/fs/data/ec/create.c
index fd0105c89..bd468e6eb 100644
--- a/fs/data/ec/create.c
+++ b/fs/data/ec/create.c
@@ -2320,6 +2320,23 @@ int bch2_stripe_repair(struct moving_context *ctxt,
 	if (!stripe_degraded(c, old_s)) {
 		event_inc_trace(c, stripe_repair_race, buf,
 				bch2_bkey_val_to_text(&buf, c, s.s_c));
+		/*
+		 * needs_reconcile is sticky: the only thing that ever cleared
+		 * it was rewriting the stripe, which we only do past the
+		 * stripe_degraded() check. A stripe flagged during a transient
+		 * device state would otherwise be reprocessed by every
+		 * reconcile pass forever, changing nothing each time.
+		 *
+		 * Clear it; the stripe trigger then drops the reconcile_hipri
+		 * work entry and the pending-stripe accounting.
+		 */
+		if (old_s->needs_reconcile) {
+			struct bkey_i_stripe *u =
+				errptr_try(bch2_bkey_make_mut_typed(trans, iter, &s.s_c, 0, stripe));
+			u->v.needs_reconcile = 0;
+			try(bch2_trans_commit(trans, NULL, NULL,
+					      BCH_TRANS_COMMIT_no_enospc));
+		}
 		return 0;
 	}
 
